  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">220000110 UNHCR Winterization Campaign Lebanon 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With the support of the Government of the Netherlands of USD 17.911.000 (C.r. 1.01: EUR 18,09 million) UNHCR is planning to assist 132,799 severely vulnerable Syrian refugee families who do not receive multi-purpose and/or food cash assistance, with winter cash assistance for three months, from December 2022 to February 2023, and 45,000 severely vulnerable Syrian refugee families who do receive cash assistance for two months. With an average household size of five persons, this means that about 268,750 severely vulnerable children, women, and men will receive lifesaving help to cover critical survival needs during the harsh winter with support from the Government of the Netherlands. Additionally, UNHCR will support families with core relief items, through a needs-based approach, such as high thermal blankets, plastic sheets, sleeping bags and winter clothes.</narrative>
  </description>
